WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.753
Your MacBook trackpad

00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:02.566
can talk with

00:00:02.378 --> 00:00:03.451
no speaker

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.287
A MacBook trackpad

00:00:05.098 --> 00:00:06.277
has no speaker

00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:07.232
just a small

00:00:07.044 --> 00:00:08.152
haptic motor that

00:00:07.964 --> 00:00:09.001
taps the glass

00:00:08.931 --> 00:00:09.768
so you feel

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.287
a click

00:00:10.822 --> 00:00:12.130
The open-source tool

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.168
NO SPEAKER drives

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:13.876
that motor up

00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:14.949
to 4,000 times

00:00:14.761 --> 00:00:15.468
a second

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:16.541
fast enough to

00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:17.579
make audible sound

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:18.546
and turns it

00:00:18.357 --> 00:00:19.206
into a voice

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:19.878
that talks

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:21.187
sings and raps

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:22.464
It is one

00:00:22.276 --> 00:00:23.573
Swift program for

00:00:23.396 --> 00:00:24.599
Apple Silicon and

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:25.424
Intel Macs

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:26.816
signed and notarized

00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:27.665
and it still

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:28.243
talks with the

00:00:28.054 --> 00:00:28.997
Mac muted

00:00:29.526 --> 00:00:30.540
Full story on

00:00:30.351 --> 00:00:31.247
the dashboard
